>>__ load "simpExtLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `add_split`

``` hol4
simpExtLib.add_split : thm -> simpExtLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adds a split rule to an extension simpset.

`add_split th ss` adds a looper applying `splitLib.SPLIT_TAC [th]`. It is
named `split name`, or `split_asm name` for an assumption rule, where
`name` is the theorem's name in the theorem database or, failing that,
the `Thy$c` name of the rule's case constant. A split looper with the
same name is replaced.

### Failure

Fails if `th` is not a split rule.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val ss = simpExtLib.add_split (splitLib.type_split_of “:'a option”)
     (simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss);
>> simpExtLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe = false} ss []
     ([], “P (case x of NONE => 0 | SOME n => n + 1) : bool”)
     (Context.snapshot());
```

